+  - `method-plus-state`: otherwise.
+
+## `conformance/scans/phpunit-assertions.jsonl`
+
+One `{"name","calls","executions"}` line per assertion name, sorted by name.
+
+- **`calls`** counts the call sites in the suites: every `.php` file (not `.blade.php`) under each repository's `tests/`, walked in sorted order. A call site is `$this->N(`, `self::N(`, `static::N(`, `parent::N(`, or `X::N(` where X resolves to `PHPUnit\Framework\Assert` or `PHPUnit\Framework\TestCase`. N must match `assert[A-Z]…` or `expect[A-Z]…`, and no declaration in the four repositories' `src/` or `tests/` may declare it as a method (compared case-insensitively). Those are Laravel's or the suites' own helpers, such as `assertDatabaseHas`. The rule also drops PHPUnit names that a Laravel class re-declares (for example `assertCount`); their `executions` still list them.
+- **`executions`** is the sum of each line's `assertions[N]` over every `conformance/inventory/<component>.jsonl` except `oracle-nondeterminism.jsonl`. A null `assertions` (a test the baseline did not run) adds nothing. These are the PHPUnit `Assert` kinds the Story 2.6 baseline recorded (FR-1).
